    "id": 3935642428,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "[P2] Make sinking rewards durable and idempotent as one settlement\n\nIf a player's hull was saved during its sinking countdown and the process stops after this payout loop but before `vessel_wreck_hull()` saves the wreck, the victor's added renown and prize claims survive while the victim reloads with its old countdown, renown, and `last_attacker`. It sinks again and awards the same renown and salvage/renown bounty a second time. The existing insurance path explicitly handles this recovery case with a marker, but `vessel_pay_prize()` uses `loss = FALSE` and the new reward path records no completed sinking. There is also an irreversible loss window because the owner's bounty is cleared at line 124 before any prize claim commits. Persist a unique sinking settlement and atomically record its claims, bounty consumption, and renown changes, so recovery can finish the wreck without issuing another reward.\n\nReviewed at `d4f5993c88ce1a8bf3f5d3c2d4e10783e51d839b`.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
