  {
    "id": 3935642539,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "[P2] Keep contraband sale prices consistent across batch sizes\n\nAt a port without a stock row, this always returns `TRADE_SUPPLY_MIN`, and `port_adjust_supply()` updates no row. However, `do_cargosell()` still calls `vessel_trade_sell_revenue()`, which increases a simulated supply after every unit within a batch. With no sale modifiers, selling 100 forbidden tomes together pays 19,942 gold; selling the same tomes one at a time pays 24,800 gold because each command starts at supply 10 again. This lets command splitting bypass the price reduction and penalizes the normal `cargosell ... all` workflow. Price every unit at the fixed scarce rate when the port does not stock the contraband, or persist demand separately from whether the port sells it, so splitting a shipment cannot change its proceeds.\n\nReviewed at `d4f5993c88ce1a8bf3f5d3c2d4e10783e51d839b`.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
