    "id": 3935642630,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "[P2] Distinguish failed stock lookups from unstocked contraband\n\n`port_stocks()` returns `FALSE` both for a missing row and for connection, prepare, execute, or fetch failures. `vessel_customs_inspection()` interprets every such result as permission to confiscate. Thus a ship returning contraband to the very port that stocks it can lose its cargo during a database failure; with 140 units and zero renown the inspection takes all units, even though that cargo should be exempt. The manifest is changed in memory before its save, so a later successful save can make the wrongful seizure permanent. Return an explicit lookup-error outcome and defer the inspection without changing cargo unless the absence of the port's stock row was successfully established.\n\nReviewed at `d4f5993c88ce1a8bf3f5d3c2d4e10783e51d839b`.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
