  {
    "id": 3935903994,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Fixed in 9c8876360.\n\n`vessel_settle_sinking()` now writes the whole settlement in one transaction: the owner's bounty is collected, each sharer's renown is saved and its prize claim queued, and the sunk hull's reduced renown is saved with her `last_attacker` set to 0. A hull saved while sinking and restored before her wreck was saved therefore reloads with no victor, finishes her wreck, and pays nothing twice. If any step fails the transaction rolls back and nothing is paid, so the bounty can no longer be lost. In-memory renown changes only after the COMMIT.\n\nSupporting changes:\n- `vessel_queue_claim()` now writes inside its caller's transaction. Insurance keeps its own transaction and its `wreck_hull` marker, and `vessel_pay_prize()` is gone.\n- `vessel_sink()` now settles before `vessel_crew_credit_kill()`, so a restored hull doesn't train the victor's crew twice either.\n\nTests (`test_vessel_rewards.c`, run against the test database):\n- The settlement saves `490:115:0,491:285:0` (her renown with `last_attacker` consumed, and the victor's renown).\n- When the claim table can't take the claim, nothing is paid: the 2,000 gold bounty stands, and neither hull's renown changes in memory or in the database.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
