  {
    "id": 3935904251,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Fixed in e1ffd9005.\n\nWhere a contraband good is not stocked, `do_cargosell()` now pays every unit the scarce price (`vessel_trade_sell_revenue()` for one unit, times the quantity). Splitting a shipment can no longer change what it earns, and the help's \"every other port pays their scarce price\" now holds for the whole batch. Persisting demand at ports that don't stock the good stays out of scope, as the S7 plan decided.\n\n`test_vessel_rewards.c` now sells 100 forbidden tomes with `cargosell forbidden all` for 24,800 gold, 100 times the single-unit sale; on `vessels-s7` this assertion fails.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
