  {
    "id": 3935904477,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Fixed in d2a1c4a22.\n\n`port_stocks()` now runs `SELECT COUNT(*)` and returns 1 (stocked), 0 (no row), or -1 (the lookup failed). Customs confiscate a lot only on 0, so a database failure lets the lot pass and leaves the cargo and manifest untouched. The market and the smugglers still treat anything but 1 as unstocked, so nobody can buy contraband during a failure either.\n\nIn `test_vessel_rewards.c`, the port's stock table is made unreadable and customs leave all 140 tomes; once it is readable again, they take all 140 as before.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
